# ORCA backend — local secrets file
# =================================
# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder, backend/.env) and fill in your own
# key below. backend/.env is read automatically when the backend starts
# (see _load_dotenv() near the top of main.py) — you never need to edit
# main.py itself, and this key is never sent anywhere except Groq's API.
#
# This powers ONLY the "AI Multi-Agent Panel" on the Agent Activity page
# (an independent LLM second-opinion on top of the existing rule-based zone
# recommendation). Every other feature in ORCA works fully without this.

# 1. Get a free Groq API key (no credit card required):
#    https://console.groq.com/keys
# 2. Paste it below, with no quotes:
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional: which Groq-hosted model to use. Left blank / unset, it defaults
# to "openai/gpt-oss-20b" — a fast free chat model. If you'd rather trade
# a bit of speed for a stronger model, try "openai/gpt-oss-120b"
# (uncomment the line below and remove the leading #).
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
#
# Groq occasionally retires model names without much notice. If the AI panel
# ever starts saying "could not be reached" again, run
# python check_groq_models.py (in this same backend folder, with the venv
# activated) to see the current list your key can use, and set GROQ_MODEL
# to one of those instead — skip the whisper-* (speech-to-text) and
# *-prompt-guard-* (safety filter, not general chat) entries.
